1
00:00:42,240 --> 00:00:43,600
After a comprehensive evaluation,

2
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:46,360
your performance does not meet the
company's development requirements.

3
00:00:46,360 --> 00:00:49,160
The company has decided to negotiate
the termination of your contract.

4
00:00:49,160 --> 00:00:50,360
What the hell?

5
00:00:50,840 --> 00:00:53,640
What else can you do
besides pissing me off all day?

6
00:00:58,840 --> 00:01:00,880
People nowadays are too fragile.

7
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:02,160
You can't even handle this little thing.

8
00:01:02,160 --> 00:01:04,560
Let's give the promotion quota
to someone else this time.

9
00:01:04,560 --> 00:01:05,840
What's wrong with young people
taking a little loss?

10
00:01:05,840 --> 00:01:06,840
Didn't you volunteer for it?

11
00:01:06,840 --> 00:01:07,960
Do you have a brain or not?

12
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:08,720
Did I force you?

13
00:01:08,720 --> 00:01:09,560
Who are you showing that long face to?

14
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:10,560
Nobody will want you if you leave here.

15
00:01:10,560 --> 00:01:11,800
Doing a good job is
what you're supposed to do.

16
00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:13,320
Give first before talking about returns.

17
00:01:13,320 --> 00:01:14,039
Why are you so special?

18
00:01:14,039 --> 00:01:15,320
I'm doing this for your own good.

19
00:01:15,320 --> 00:01:17,180
There are no unachievable goals.

20
00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:21,690
No matter how hard it is,

21
00:01:21,760 --> 00:01:23,240
Mom and Dad will buy you
an apartment in the city.

22
00:01:23,240 --> 00:01:24,360
Is the client looking at you
or the proposal?

23
00:01:24,360 --> 00:01:25,800
Can you at least pretend a little better?

24
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:26,760
Why wasn't it completed?

25
00:01:26,760 --> 00:01:27,640
The key performance indicators
this time...

26
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:30,039
You can't even take this little grievance?

27
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:32,860
You can't even handle this little thing.

28
00:01:37,880 --> 00:01:39,539
We can't hit innocent people.

29
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:05,200
Why should wage slaves
make things hard for each other?

30
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:07,930
I shouldn't add to
the cleaning lady's workload.

31
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:12,280
Tangtang,

32
00:02:12,280 --> 00:02:13,640
I've heard you resigned.

33
00:02:13,640 --> 00:02:15,720
I've been sick of
that crappy company for a long time.

34
00:02:15,720 --> 00:02:16,680
The 996 schedule, exploiting people,

35
00:02:16,680 --> 00:02:17,720
and shifting the blame.

36
00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:19,180
It's a good thing you left.

37
00:02:19,560 --> 00:02:20,840
News travels so fast.

38
00:02:20,840 --> 00:02:22,640
That manager Hu

39
00:02:22,640 --> 00:02:24,680
said you were incompetent.

40
00:02:24,920 --> 00:02:26,720
He just wanted an excuse to fire you

41
00:02:26,720 --> 00:02:27,160
and

42
00:02:27,160 --> 00:02:29,960
make room for his newly graduated niece.

43
00:02:31,680 --> 00:02:33,320
Forget it. I'm tired.

44
00:02:33,320 --> 00:02:34,480
I can't hustle anymore.

45
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:35,840
Ever since graduation,

46
00:02:36,560 --> 00:02:38,800
I've been working mechanically every day,

47
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:40,360
only to go home and work more overtime.

48
00:02:40,360 --> 00:02:40,760
I don't even know

49
00:02:40,760 --> 00:02:42,760
what the meaning of life is anymore.

50
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:47,160
I used to believe that hard work pays off.

51
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:49,160
But now I realize

52
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:51,320
hard work is just the ticket.

53
00:02:51,720 --> 00:02:53,880
Winning still depends on luck.

54
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:56,600
I used to have expectations too.

55
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:58,320
But every expectation in life

56
00:02:58,320 --> 00:02:59,850
just ends up destroying me.

57
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:02,680
My bestie would never say something

58
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:04,360
so poetic and depressing.

59
00:03:04,440 --> 00:03:05,600
I don't care who you are.

60
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:06,920
Get out of my bestie's body right now.

61
00:03:06,920 --> 00:03:07,920
Back off! Back off! Back off!

62
00:03:07,920 --> 00:03:09,360
I can't explain it to you. I'm hanging up.

63
00:03:09,360 --> 00:03:10,360
Wait, wait, wait.

64
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:12,800
I know you're in a bad mood right now,

65
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:13,520
but please don't

66
00:03:13,520 --> 00:03:15,040
psych yourself out.

67
00:03:15,240 --> 00:03:16,200
Do you remember?

68
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:18,800
I opened a youth retirement home

69
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:20,200
called Yunbianshang

70
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:22,200
by the sea of clouds
in Xiayanbei, Xinchang.

71
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:24,600
I have to go on a long business trip
for a few days.

72
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:27,000
Can you come over
and help me look after it?

73
00:03:27,840 --> 00:03:30,440
Open the window of my place,
and there's the sea of clouds.

74
00:03:30,440 --> 00:03:31,960
Behind it is a tea plantation.

75
00:03:31,960 --> 00:03:34,840
You can water flowers
and brew tea every day,

76
00:03:34,920 --> 00:03:37,160
and lie in the yard
counting stars at night.

77
00:03:37,160 --> 00:03:38,200
How romantic!

78
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:40,480
The feng shui in Xiayanbei, Xinchang
is nourishing.

79
00:03:40,480 --> 00:03:43,160
You definitely won't wither away here.

80
00:03:44,079 --> 00:03:47,010
If I could rest in peace
in a heavenly place like that,

81
00:03:47,640 --> 00:03:49,040
not bothering anyone,

82
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:51,440
just quietly becoming nutrients
for the mountains...

83
00:03:51,440 --> 00:03:52,840
that sounds pretty nice.

84
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:55,440
Okay, send me the address.

85
00:04:00,360 --> 00:04:02,160
Tang Jialing has really made it.

86
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:03,640
She opened a nursing home

87
00:04:03,680 --> 00:04:04,280
and can even afford

88
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:06,080
such an imposing security team.

89
00:04:06,720 --> 00:04:07,650
Hold on a second.

90
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:08,840
Hello.

91
00:04:08,960 --> 00:04:10,600
Listen, lady,

92
00:04:10,600 --> 00:04:12,240
we're debt collectors.

93
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:18,880
Please, guys.

94
00:04:20,519 --> 00:04:22,400
Have some mercy.

95
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:23,800
Give me a little more time.

96
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:25,400
I'm a bit tight on cash lately.

97
00:04:25,400 --> 00:04:26,440
In a month,

98
00:04:26,440 --> 00:04:29,360
I promise to wire the money
to your accounts.

99
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:32,200
This is your friend, right?

100
00:04:32,200 --> 00:04:33,680
Listen to me, pay up right now.

101
00:04:33,680 --> 00:04:34,280
If you don't, I'll take her--

102
00:04:34,280 --> 00:04:35,120
No, no, bro.

103
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:38,800
It has nothing to do with me.

104
00:04:39,120 --> 00:04:42,120
I'm just here to retire.

105
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:49,480
You're so young, and you're retiring?

106
00:04:49,880 --> 00:04:51,600
Who are you kidding?

107
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:53,260
Do you think I'd believe that?

108
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:54,800
Wait a minute.

109
00:04:55,280 --> 00:04:56,840
Aren't I here to seek death?

110
00:04:57,200 --> 00:04:58,260
What am I afraid of?

111
00:04:59,840 --> 00:05:01,120
Believe it or not.

112
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:03,760
I have no money, but you can take my life.

113
00:05:03,760 --> 00:05:05,520
Come on. Kill me for the debt.

114
00:05:05,520 --> 00:05:06,120
Come on!

115
00:05:06,120 --> 00:05:07,240
Take out your knives and axes

116
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:08,480
and hack at my head.

117
00:05:08,480 --> 00:05:09,600
Come on, chop right here.

118
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:10,240
Don't hold back.

119
00:05:10,240 --> 00:05:11,370
Please just kill me,

120
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:13,680
okay?

121
00:05:16,280 --> 00:05:17,080
Are you trying

122
00:05:17,640 --> 00:05:18,480
to scam us?

123
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:19,840
We live in a civilized society.

124
00:05:19,840 --> 00:05:21,640
You have to obey the law, right?

125
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:23,760
We're collecting debts legally.

126
00:05:23,760 --> 00:05:25,360
We don't do that mafia stuff.

127
00:05:31,240 --> 00:05:32,080
You just need a month,

128
00:05:32,080 --> 00:05:33,120
right?

129
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:34,320
One month it is.

130
00:05:34,440 --> 00:05:35,159
Let's go, let's go.

131
00:05:35,159 --> 00:05:36,159
What a freak.

132
00:05:36,159 --> 00:05:36,840
Let's go.

133
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:40,000
Sir, don't run!

134
00:05:40,320 --> 00:05:42,000
I can sign a waiver.

135
00:05:46,120 --> 00:05:48,000
I really have no other choice right now.

136
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:50,360
Can you just give me one more month?

137
00:05:50,360 --> 00:05:51,240
Don't worry.

138
00:05:51,520 --> 00:05:53,640
I'm already raising funds

139
00:05:53,760 --> 00:05:55,280
on Wall Street.

140
00:05:55,600 --> 00:05:56,480
Once I get the money,

141
00:05:56,480 --> 00:05:58,540
I'll come back to save you right away.

142
00:05:58,720 --> 00:06:00,920
It's all my damn ex-boyfriend's fault.

143
00:06:01,040 --> 00:06:01,640
He insisted on borrowing money.

144
00:06:01,640 --> 00:06:03,360
He claimed he wanted
to expand the nursing home,

145
00:06:03,360 --> 00:06:05,680
and secretly borrowed it under my name.

146
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:09,360
In the end, the jerk ran off,
and the debt can't be paid.

147
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:11,560
Isn't this

148
00:06:11,560 --> 00:06:12,960
your favorite dress?

149
00:06:13,440 --> 00:06:14,680
Your boyfriend, Zhang Yi,

150
00:06:14,680 --> 00:06:17,000
thought this gown was
too expensive back then.

151
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:19,680
He said you should just rent it for a day.

152
00:06:20,120 --> 00:06:21,520
I've already bought it.

153
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:22,760
That's the spirit.

154
00:06:22,760 --> 00:06:25,000
We independent women get what we want.

155
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:26,880
Does Zhang Yi

156
00:06:27,480 --> 00:06:29,160
know you lost your job?

157
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:32,000
If his family finds out,

158
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:33,560
they'll flip out.

159
00:06:37,960 --> 00:06:39,480
The moment I lost my job,

160
00:06:40,440 --> 00:06:42,040
I also lost my relationship.

161
00:06:42,760 --> 00:06:43,840
Why didn't you meet

162
00:06:43,840 --> 00:06:44,880
the KPI this time?

163
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:46,159
Answer me.

164
00:06:47,880 --> 00:06:49,000
Eight million

165
00:06:49,360 --> 00:06:52,520
was an impossible target to begin with.

166
00:06:52,520 --> 00:06:54,280
There are no impossible targets.

167
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:56,340
Pack your things and leave right now.

168
00:07:01,520 --> 00:07:02,000
Isn't this

169
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:04,240
the highlighter you've been saving?

170
00:07:04,240 --> 00:07:05,560
You actually used it today.

171
00:07:05,560 --> 00:07:07,420
Living like there's no tomorrow?

172
00:07:07,880 --> 00:07:09,560
I rarely use it,

173
00:07:09,920 --> 00:07:11,450
so there's still a lot left.

174
00:07:12,840 --> 00:07:13,520
Forget it.

175
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:15,740
I'll just mix it with my ashes.

176
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:19,640
I'm gonna be the most dazzling person
in the underworld.

177
00:07:19,640 --> 00:07:21,200
You're hilarious, sis.

178
00:07:21,480 --> 00:07:23,520
Honestly, where are you going

179
00:07:23,560 --> 00:07:24,600
dressed up like this?

180
00:07:24,600 --> 00:07:25,400
A date?

181
00:07:28,680 --> 00:07:29,720
I'm going to die.

182
00:07:30,440 --> 00:07:32,560
You're as funny as ever.

183
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:34,800
Oh my god.

184
00:07:34,840 --> 00:07:35,760
My phone.

185
00:07:35,840 --> 00:07:36,720
Give it to me.

186
00:07:56,040 --> 00:07:57,120
This is so nice.

187
00:07:58,600 --> 00:08:01,440
The tea garden smells so good.

188
00:08:14,120 --> 00:08:14,880
Qingqing,

189
00:08:14,960 --> 00:08:17,000
why did you send us so much money?

190
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:18,480
Your mom and I have enough.

191
00:08:18,640 --> 00:08:20,440
We took on another part-time job

192
00:08:20,560 --> 00:08:23,160
to buy you a new house
before you get married.

193
00:08:24,440 --> 00:08:26,960
My parents already know you got fired.

194
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:28,400
You're an outsider.

195
00:08:28,760 --> 00:08:30,880
They didn't want us together
in the first place.

196
00:08:30,880 --> 00:08:32,520
And now you've lost your job.

197
00:08:32,880 --> 00:08:34,400
They're forcing me to break up with you.

198
00:08:34,400 --> 00:08:36,200
Let's stop contacting each other for now.

199
00:08:36,200 --> 00:08:38,059
We'll talk when you find a new job.

200
00:08:41,720 --> 00:08:43,000
Why did you unfollow me?

201
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:43,760
Did I do something wrong?

202
00:08:43,760 --> 00:08:44,640
Do you like someone else?

203
00:08:44,640 --> 00:08:45,700
You're my only fan.

204
00:08:49,560 --> 00:08:51,960
The annual blame-shifting conference
is on again.

205
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:54,160
As a corporate slave
in a big tech company,

206
00:08:54,160 --> 00:08:56,080
I can only slack off and watch the drama.

207
00:08:56,080 --> 00:08:57,960
I'm not taking the blame for this.

208
00:08:58,160 --> 00:08:59,640
How can you blame us for this?

209
00:08:59,640 --> 00:09:02,000
Our budget is already
much higher than our peers'.

210
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:04,360
It's obviously your proposal
that has problems.

211
00:09:04,360 --> 00:09:07,220
Customers don't even have the desire
to click on it.

212
00:09:10,400 --> 00:09:10,880
What's going on?

213
00:09:10,880 --> 00:09:11,640
Who is it?

214
00:09:11,680 --> 00:09:13,040
So arrogant. What is this?

215
00:09:13,040 --> 00:09:14,360
Watching this kind of video in the office?

216
00:09:14,360 --> 00:09:15,760
Someone must have connected
to the wrong computer.

217
00:09:15,760 --> 00:09:17,000
What on earth is this?

218
00:09:17,080 --> 00:09:18,040
Who's watching this?

219
00:09:18,040 --> 00:09:18,600
Who?

220
00:09:19,840 --> 00:09:20,800
Who is this?

221
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:23,800
How can they watch this kind of stuff
in the office?

222
00:09:27,800 --> 00:09:29,330
Whenever I feel exhausted,

223
00:09:29,960 --> 00:09:32,120
your videos always give me strength.

224
00:09:33,480 --> 00:09:35,920
It's a pity I didn't get to see
you become a big star,

225
00:09:35,920 --> 00:09:38,650
but thank you for being with me
through this time.

226
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:42,640
I'll continue to support you
in my next life.

227
00:09:51,360 --> 00:09:54,520
Peace and quiet at last.

228
00:09:56,760 --> 00:09:57,960
Is this your phone?

229
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:02,120
Yes, it is.

230
00:10:02,680 --> 00:10:03,680
Thank you so much.

231
00:10:06,640 --> 00:10:07,640
It just hit me.

232
00:10:08,640 --> 00:10:10,160
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to.

233
00:10:10,160 --> 00:10:11,800
I just found this phone too annoying,

234
00:10:11,800 --> 00:10:12,920
so I tossed it,

235
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:14,880
and...

236
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:17,860
What are you doing lying here?

237
00:10:18,920 --> 00:10:21,640
I saw this place is backed by mountains
and faces the water.

238
00:10:21,640 --> 00:10:22,680
It's beautiful,

239
00:10:22,760 --> 00:10:24,490
clearly a great feng shui spot.

240
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:25,640
So,

241
00:10:26,720 --> 00:10:28,250
I want to rest in peace here.

242
00:10:28,480 --> 00:10:30,210
This is my family's tea garden.

243
00:10:30,920 --> 00:10:31,560
I'm sorry.

244
00:10:31,560 --> 00:10:32,520
If you mind,

245
00:10:32,560 --> 00:10:33,800
I can find another place.

246
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:35,120
You can't do it anywhere.

247
00:10:35,120 --> 00:10:36,240
We're about to be evaluated

248
00:10:36,240 --> 00:10:37,840
as a provincial beautiful village
demonstration site.

249
00:10:37,840 --> 00:10:40,500
You can't commit suicide
anywhere around here.

250
00:10:40,760 --> 00:10:42,490
Why are there KPIs everywhere?

251
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:44,240
I'll leave then.

252
00:10:44,240 --> 00:10:45,900
I won't cause you any trouble.

253
00:10:50,800 --> 00:10:51,800
You don't know me.

254
00:10:58,320 --> 00:11:00,880
Should we know each other?

255
00:11:04,840 --> 00:11:07,240
It's fine.
We can get to know each other now.

256
00:11:07,760 --> 00:11:09,440
Hello, I'm Yun Qingqing.

257
00:11:10,880 --> 00:11:11,720
Yun Qingqing,

258
00:11:13,960 --> 00:11:15,560
I'll be keeping an eye on you.

259
00:11:15,640 --> 00:11:18,040
Don't even think about
dying in front of me.

260
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:32,730
Gu Hai

261
00:11:33,680 --> 00:11:34,040
Shi Zheng

262
00:11:34,040 --> 00:11:34,500
Zhu Zifo

263
00:11:36,280 --> 00:11:37,010
Zhang Yanyan

264
00:11:45,840 --> 00:11:46,370
He Lijian

265
00:11:46,480 --> 00:11:47,340
Liu Chengcheng

266
00:11:47,480 --> 00:11:48,340
Chang Zhicheng

267
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:50,640
Li Jiakang

268
00:11:52,280 --> 00:11:52,940
Zhao Xinran

269
00:11:54,200 --> 00:11:54,840
Xin Xiaoqing

270
00:11:54,840 --> 00:11:55,640
Zhang Xiaojie

271
00:11:55,800 --> 00:11:56,440
Wu Changling

272
00:11:56,440 --> 00:11:57,240
Zhong Shangyu

273
00:11:58,040 --> 00:11:58,640
Sui Yugang

274
00:11:59,320 --> 00:11:59,920
Sun Wenyan

275
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:10,730
He Cuiyan

276
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:13,040
You Weiyun

277
00:12:13,040 --> 00:12:13,500
Han Bing

278
00:12:14,680 --> 00:12:15,000
Yang Yunshu

